Description: Upload-only Google Drive folder
 CloudDrop uploads everything you put in ~/CloudDrop to Google Drive, with the
 same folder structure. Deleting a file on your computer never deletes it in
 Drive: it becomes cloud-only and can be downloaded back at any time, so you
 can free up space without losing anything. Space can also be freed
 automatically some days after upload.
 .
 It includes a desktop app with a setup assistant, a file browser and an
 activity history, a top-bar status icon, status icons and actions in GNOME
 Files, and a background service that resumes interrupted uploads.
